{"id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics#lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-derivatives","title":"lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-derivatives","path":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics.md","line":181,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics.tex#lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-derivatives","uses":["[[references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics#lem:chow-iii-space-time-convolution-associative]]","[[references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics#lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-first-derivative]]","[[references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics#lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-second-derivative]]","[[references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics#lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-time-derivative]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics.tex","label":"lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-derivatives","line":333,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[Covariant derivatives of the convolution series]\n\\label{lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-derivatives}\n\\source{chow-et-al-ricci-flow-part-iii:page-0298,chow-et-al-ricci-flow-part-iii:page-0299}\n\\uses{lem:chow-iii-space-time-convolution-associative, lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-first-derivative, lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-second-derivative, lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-time-derivative}\n\\dcref{ch24:24.19}\n\\group{Convolution Series}\n\n\nIf \\(m,\\ell\\ge0\\) and \\(N>n/2+2\\ell+m\\), then\n\\[\n \\sum_{k=1}^\\infty\n \\partial_\\tau^\\ell\\nabla_x^m\\bigl((L_{x,\\tau}P_N)^{*k}\\bigr)\n\\]\nconverges absolutely and uniformly.  Thus its derivatives may be taken\ntermwise.  Consequently\n\\[\n H=P_N+P_N*\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty(L_{x,\\tau}P_N)^{*k}\n\\]\nis a smooth fundamental solution.\n\\end{lemma}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[Covariant derivatives of the convolution series] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a63686f772d6969692d706172616d65747269782d636f6e766f6c7574696f6e2d6465726976617469766573\"></span> <span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">chow-et-al-ricci-flow-part-iii:page-0298, chow-et-al-ricci-flow-part-iii:page-0299</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FChowEtAl%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics%23lem%3Achow-iii-space-time-convolution-associative\">↗ lem:chow-iii-space-time-convolution-associative</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FChowEtAl%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics%23lem%3Achow-iii-parametrix-convolution-first-derivative\">↗ lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-first-derivative</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FChowEtAl%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics%23lem%3Achow-iii-parametrix-convolution-second-derivative\">↗ lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-second-derivative</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FChowEtAl%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics%23lem%3Achow-iii-parametrix-convolution-time-derivative\">↗ lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-time-derivative</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch24:24.19</span></span>\\group Convolution Series <p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$m,\\ell \\ge 0$\">$m,\\ell \\ge 0$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$N&gt;n/2+2\\ell +m$\">$N&gt;n/2+2\\ell +m$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\sum _{k=1}^\\infty \\partial _\\tau ^\\ell \\nabla _x^m\\bigl((L_{x,\\tau }P_N)^{*k}\\bigr)  \\]\">\\[  \\sum _{k=1}^\\infty \\partial _\\tau ^\\ell \\nabla _x^m\\bigl((L_{x,\\tau }P_N)^{*k}\\bigr)  \\]</span> converges absolutely and uniformly. Thus its derivatives may be taken termwise. Consequently <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  H=P_N+P_N*\\sum _{k=1}^\\infty (L_{x,\\tau }P_N)^{*k}  \\]\">\\[  H=P_N+P_N*\\sum _{k=1}^\\infty (L_{x,\\tau }P_N)^{*k}  \\]</span> is a smooth fundamental solution. ","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: group"]},"previous":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics#lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-time-derivative","next":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics#thm:chow-iii-evolving-heat-kernel-expansion","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics#lem:chow-iii-space-time-convolution-associative","title":"lem:chow-iii-space-time-convolution-associative","label":"lem:chow-iii-space-time-convolution-associative"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics#lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-first-derivative","title":"lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-first-derivative","label":"lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-first-derivative"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics#lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-second-derivative","title":"lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-second-derivative","label":"lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-second-derivative"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch24-heat-kernel-evolving-metrics#lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-time-derivative","title":"lem:chow-iii-parametrix-convolution-time-derivative","label":"lem:chow-iii-par